markdown <<MARKDOWN
<div style="max-width:1000px; margin:0 auto; font-family:ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial; background:#FFFFFF; padding:32px; color:#292F36; line-height:1.6; font-size:16px;">

<!-- Card Wrapper -->
<div style="border-radius:18px; overflow:hidden; box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(41,47,54,0.08); border:1px solid #e3e6ea;">

<!-- Header -->
<div style="background:#8C52BA; padding:26px;">
<div style="color:#FFFFFF; font-size:26px; font-weight:800;">
Pitfall 1: Treating AI Like It Has Awareness of the Current World
</div>
</div>

<!-- Light Grey Content Band -->
<div style="background:#F4F6F8; padding:36px;">

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap:32px;">

<!-- LEFT COLUMN -->
<div>
<div style="border:1px solid #dfe3e8; border-radius:18px; padding:24px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(41,47,54,0.04);">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:20px; margin-bottom:14px; color:#0093A4;">
Scenario
</div>

<div style="margin-bottom:18px;">
Ms. Alvarez, a 10th-grade civics teacher in Arizona, asks an AI tool on Monday morning:
</div>

<div style="background:#F7F8FA; border-left:5px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:14px; padding:18px; margin-bottom:18px;">
<div style="font-size:14px; font-weight:700; color:#8C52BA; margin-bottom:8px;">
Prompt to AI
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:600;">
“Create a warm-up activity about the major election news happening this week.”
</div>
</div>

<div>
The AI generates a discussion prompt about the Iowa caucuses and early primary voting. Ms. Alvarez copies it into her slide deck without double-checking. During class, a student says, “That already happened months ago.” The class loses confidence, and time is spent explaining the error instead of discussing civics.
</div>

</div>
</div>

<!-- RIGHT COLUMN -->
<div>

<div style="border:1px solid #dfe3e8; border-radius:18px; padding:24px; margin-bottom:24px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(41,47,54,0.04);">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:20px; margin-bottom:12px; color:#ED6060;">
The Pitfall
</div>
<div>
Assuming the AI understands what “this week,” “today,” or “right now” refer to in the real world.
</div>
</div>

<div style="border:1px solid #dfe3e8; border-radius:18px; padding:24px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(41,47,54,0.04);">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:20px; margin-bottom:12px; color:#0093A4;">
Quick Tip
</div>

<div style="margin-bottom:18px;">
If timing matters, always specify the exact date, event, or context instead of assuming the AI knows what is current.
</div>

<div style="background:#F7F8FA; border-left:5px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:14px; padding:18px;">
<div style="font-size:14px; font-weight:700; color:#8C52BA; margin-bottom:8px;">
Safer Prompt Example
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:600;">
“Create a warm-up activity about major U.S. election news for the week of <b>March 4–8, 2026</b>. Include 3 discussion questions.”
</div>
</div>

</div>
</div>

</div>

<!-- Under the Hood -->
<div style="margin-top:32px;">
<details style="border:1px solid #dfe3e8; border-radius:18px; background:#FFFFFF; overflow:hidden; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(41,47,54,0.04);">
<summary style="cursor:pointer; padding:20px; font-weight:800; font-size:20px; color:#0093A4;">
What’s Going on Under the Hood
</summary>
<div style="padding:0 20px 20px 20px; border-top:1px solid #F4F6F8;">
The AI does not have built-in awareness of the current date, live events, or what is happening “this week” unless it is explicitly given that information. It generates responses based on patterns in training data, not real-time understanding. When a prompt includes time-based language, the model fills in what is statistically likely to fit that phrase, which may reflect outdated or generalized examples rather than the present moment.
</div>
</details>
</div>

</div>
</div>
</div>

MARKDOWN
